      "content": "It can be nuanced. If you're independently creating a new data pipeline from scratch using a structure or method that's a common industry practice, and there are no identical or too closely similar structures or methods to the confidential information from the client, this might be considered just general knowledge or a \"scorn\" (harmless groan) of previous work experience.\n\nHowever, using any specific and unique structures, configurations, algorithms, or detailed approaches you've encountered at the client could potentially be considered proprietary, revealing confidential information. Always document your thought process and decisions to prove they were independently developed in your own domain of expertise. If there's any doubt, consult with a legal professional. It's the best way to safeguard yourself against intellectual property claims that might arise from using similar logic or structure unknowingly derived from your prior work. General patterns recognized in the industry on their own are typically safe, but you should always err on the side of caution and steer clear of specifics.",
